p"><h2 class="sr-only select-none">You said: Hold off on that for now.</h2><div class="flex flex-col items-end gap-1"><div data-user-message-bubble="true" class="group relative inline-flex gap-2 bg-bg-300 rounded-xl pl-2.5 py-2.5 break-words text-text-100 transition-all max-w-[75ch] flex-col !px-4 max-w-[85%]" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="flex flex-row gap-2 relative"><div class="flex-1"><div data-testid="user-message" class="font-large !font-user-message py-0.5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 relative [&amp;_ul]:!space-y-0 [&amp;_ol]:!space-y-0 [&amp;_ul]:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]:pl-8" style="max-height: none; overflow: hidden; position: relative;"><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Hold off on that for now. I have another project. Write a children's book called the adventures of Peter Par-rat. Peter should be a fun-loving creature that was created by an absent minded, but lovable geneticist who accidentally created Peter trying to find a cure for a unnamed terminal illness. Peter is learning about the world around him. Include underlying Christian themes and moral implications with regard to creation and human intervention in the process. Please add illustrations as well. I would like this to be a series of Children's books that can be serialized. The story should be the typical length of a Children's book geared towards 6-12 year olds. Here's an image for reference.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 pointer-coarse:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><span class="text-text-500 text-xs flex items-center mr-2">May 14</span><div class="flex items-center"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none border-0 outline-none rounded h