<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>You need to delete the README.md. Here's how:</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <strong><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">github.com/stefanisrighting/logosandlife</code></strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click on <strong><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">README.md</code></strong> in the file list</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click the <strong>three dots <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">...</code></strong> menu (top right of the file view)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>"Delete file"</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>"Commit changes"</strong> → <strong>"Commit directly to main"</strong> → <strong>Commit</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Wait about 60 seconds</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Refresh <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">stefanisrighting.github.io/logosandlife</code></li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">That's the only thing standing between you and a live app. The <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">index.html</code> is already there and ready — Jekyll is just prioritizing the README over it. Once the README is gone, your app loads automatically.</p>
