<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Option A — Add a <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">_config.yml</code> to disable Jekyll (fastest)</h3>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">github.com/stefanisrighting/logosandlife</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Add file → Create new file</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Name it exactly: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">.nojekyll</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Leave the content completely blank</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Commit new file</strong></li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Then also:
6. Click on your <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">index.html</code> file
7. Click the <strong>pencil ✏️ edit icon</strong>
8. Don't change anything — just scroll down and click <strong>Commit changes</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">This forces GitHub to stop using Jekyll and serve your HTML file directly.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Option B — Use Netlify Drop instead (2 minutes, zero friction)</h3>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <strong><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">app.netlify.com/drop</code></strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Drag your <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">logos_and_life_v2.html</code> file (renamed to <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">index.html</code>) onto the page</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Get a live URL instantly — no account needed</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">You can claim a custom name like <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">logosandlife.netlify.app</code></li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">This bypasses GitHub entirely and just works. Many developers prefer it for single HTML file apps exactly like yours.</p>
